  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the text expressing offense",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'how dare people make fun of our peaceful religion', which frames the user as someone who is outraged or offended by mockery of Buddhism. The text implicitly addresses the viewer as 'you' — the person seeing the meme — by using 'how dare people make fun' as a rhetorical device that invokes the viewer's own moral stance or identity as a defender of the religion. The projection is onto the text_chunk, which acts as the vehicle for the user's imagined emotional response.",
